- Story & Context: Mara admitted to the other commuters that she wasn't actually heading to work, but rather chasing the specific resonant frequency of the bridge crossing the southern marshes. She confessed that her pocket synth was stolen from a dying botanist in the carriage last winter, and every melody she played was an attempt to replicate his last, fading heartbeat. The confession left the carriage silent, save for the rhythmic clatter of wheels hitting a loose joint. "I am just a sequence searching for a home."
