Track 3: Grafting the Iron Root
- Story & Context: Legend says the station at Oakhaven is haunted by the sound of music that never stops, a perpetual cycle of bass and birdsong that keeps the vines from reclaiming the platform. Travelers claim that if you stand on the yellow line at exactly 3:00 AM, the station speakers play the final, unreleased symphony of the night-train collective. It is said that the roots of the platform have fused with the electrical grid, creating a self-sustaining ecosystem of sound that has outlived the city itself. "The iron holds the memory of the vine."
